      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Original game sprites for Gouden Horizon, a climate-action RPG set in postapocalyptic Netherlands 2089. Smooth polished hand-painted fantasy action-RPG art inspired by Torchlight: full readable volumes, brass, teal, weathered salvage, warm upper-left key light and soft cool fill. Broad sculptural painterly forms, detailed tangible salvaged materials, clear silhouettes. No pixel art, no vector art, no photorealism. Genuine transparent RGBA background, including transparent negative space between sprites. No backdrop, no scenery beyond the explicitly requested object, no ground tile, no text, no labels, no grid lines, no watermark. Each entire sprite including held weapons, shadows and glow fits well within its own cell's central 70 percent, leaving generous transparent margins all around. No part crosses any cell boundary.\nAsset type: production game travel/camp sprite atlas. EXACTLY 1536 by 1024 pixels, a strict invisible 3-column by 2-row grid of 512 by 512 cells. Six distinct isolated sprite groups with evenly spaced cell centers: (256,256),(768,256),(1280,256),(256,768),(768,768),(1280,768). Elevated three-quarter game camera, consistent perspective.\nRow 1 left: weathered brass-and-wood low transit gate, small cyan lamp, modest gate height about 1.4 humans, open traversable center, practical Dutch floodland salvage architecture.\nRow 1 middle: overgrown stone-and-bronze gate, small green lamp, modest human-scale open traversable center.\nRow 1 right: industrial salvaged-metal gate, small amber lamp, modest human-scale open traversable center.\nRow 2 left: slim maritime doorway/frame with teal light, modest human-scale open traversable center.\nRow 2 middle: safe camp trade stall, small warm canvas awning, crates and brass tools, a friendly female trader standing directly beside this small stall. She belongs to the stall sprite group and is fully contained in that cell.\nRow 2 right: compact salvaged forge workbench with a warm furnace and a warm crystal.\nAll gates are real doorway structures with low construction and passable open centers, never magical circular portals. Tiny contained contact shadows, all lamps/glow restrained to each cell. Complete objects, no cropping.",
