      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Original game sprites for Gouden Horizon, a climate-action RPG set in postapocalyptic Netherlands 2089. Smooth polished hand-painted fantasy action-RPG art inspired by Torchlight: full readable volumes, brass, teal, weathered salvage, warm upper-left key light and soft cool fill. Broad sculptural painterly forms, detailed tangible salvaged materials, clear silhouettes. No pixel art, no vector art, no photorealism. Genuine transparent RGBA background, including transparent negative space between sprites. No backdrop, no scenery beyond the explicitly requested object, no ground tile, no text, no labels, no grid lines, no watermark. Each entire sprite including held weapons, shadows and glow fits well within its own cell's central 70 percent, leaving generous transparent margins all around. No part crosses any cell boundary.\nAsset type: production equipment sprite atlas, twelve distinct item sprites. EXACTLY 1536 by 1536 pixels. Strict invisible 4-column by 3-row layout, cells384 pixels wide and512 pixels high. Cell centers row1 (192,256),(576,256),(960,256),(1344,256), row2 (192,768),(576,768),(960,768),(1344,768), row3 (192,1280),(576,1280),(960,1280),(1344,1280). Put items in EXACTLY this row-major order. Each complete object fits central70% of its own rectangular cell, generous real transparent margins. Elevated three-quarter view. Equipment without people or mannequins.\nRow1 column1 / item0: simple salvaged duct-tape metal focus rod, grey metal with a small teal crystal; include the entire long rod.\nRow1 column2 / item1: sturdy navy utility coat with small brass clips, coat displayed as an isolated empty garment.\nRow1 column3 / item2: battered grey field compass relic, compact round mechanical instrument.\nRow1 column4 / item3: green crystal fork focus on a brass handle, include entire fork and handle.\nRow2 column1 / item4: plum-and-teal insulated ranger jacket, isolated empty garment.\nRow2 column2 / item5: golden cracked sun compass mechanical relic, warm gold compass with a sun motif, a crack and teal accents.\nRow2 column3 / item6: plain worn brown field boots, one recognizably coordinated pair grouped together.\nRow2 column4 / item7: simple sturdy brown work gloves, one coordinated pair grouped together.\nRow3 column1 / item8: compact salvage utility belt with grey pouches, complete small belt.\nRow3 column2 / item9: teal-and-gold insulated fast-travel boots, one coordinated pair, upgraded distinctive shapes.\nRow3 column3 / item10: copper-and-teal storm-casting gloves, one coordinated pair with restrained luminous teal detail.\nRow3 column4 / item11: warm brass solar belt with a small crystal core, complete belt and gold central mechanism.\nConsistent original gear style and recognizable common/uncommon base shapes. No person, mannequin, backdrop, captions, label, lettering, grid, separate decorative elements or shadow outside cells.",
